    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (2/2 tests pass, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key and the duplicate-detection rules exactly as the spec requires.\n\n**New / reworked pieces (each a small unit with one responsibility):**\n\n- **`Soundex`** \u2014 computes the American Soundex code of a name (handles the vowel-reset and `H`/`W`-transparent adjacency rules). Reused by both the identity key and the soft-match detector.\n- **`Sha256`** \u2014 a shared lower-case hex SHA-256 helper. The hashing logic that was privately duplicated inside `Households` now lives here and is used by both `Households` and `OwnerIdentity` (no copy-paste).\n- **`OwnerIdentity.key()`** \u2014 now returns `SHA-256hex(normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))` (previously an un-hashed `telephone|email|householdId` string).\n- **`DuplicateIdentityValidator` + `DuplicateIdentityException`** \u2014 the single 409 duplicate check, keyed on the identity key over non-deleted owners.\n- **`PossibleDuplicateDetector`** \u2014 soft match now fires when the identity key **differs** but `soundex(lastName)` **and** postcode match.\n\n**Behavioural changes wired in:**\n\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` now calls `duplicateIdentityValidator.validate(owner)` instead of the household-duplicate block. `householdId` is still computed (it feeds the household-size membership rules), but it no longer drives duplicate rejection.\n- Because telephone is part of the key, two owners with the same last name + postcode but **different telephones** now produce a soft match rather than a 409.\n- The email-domain blocklist still runs first (it's a `@Valid` binder validator, before the controller body), and deleted owners are still ignored in both the hard and soft checks.\n- Removed the now-dead `HouseholdDuplicateValidator` / `HouseholdDuplicateException`, updated `ExceptionControllerAdvice` to map the new exception to 409, and refreshed the `openapi.yml` docs for `identityKey`, `sharesHousehold`, and `possibleDuplicate*`.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` \u2014 64-hex shape; `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` \u2014 identical identity \u2192 409) pass, along with the full suite.",
